# Strategy 5 — MACD Boolean Cross Trading
#
# Showcase for the Tier B MACD boolean primitives. Where
# macd-breakout.strat builds entry/exit conditions out of arithmetic
# expressions on macd_line / macd_signal, this strategy uses the
# pre-detected boolean primitives directly: macd_bullish_cross,
# macd_bearish_cross, macd_zero_cross_up, macd_zero_cross_down.
# rsi_crosses_50 is layered as a momentum filter on entries.

Feature: MACD Boolean Cross Trading
  Primary timeframe: 1h
  Parameter stop_loss_pct default 2
  Parameter take_profit_pct default 5

  Scenario: Enter long on MACD bullish cross with RSI confirmation
    Given no open position
    When macd_bullish_cross()
    And rsi_crosses_50()
    Then long_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 - stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 + take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit long on MACD zero cross down
    Given a long position is open
    When macd_zero_cross_down()
    Then long_exit

  Scenario: Enter short on MACD bearish cross with RSI confirmation
    Given no open position
    When macd_bearish_cross()
    And rsi_crosses_50()
    Then short_entry
    And with stop_loss at entry_price * (1 + stop_loss_pct / 100)
    And with take_profit at entry_price * (1 - take_profit_pct / 100)

  Scenario: Exit short on MACD zero cross up
    Given a short position is open
    When macd_zero_cross_up()
    Then short_exit
